{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>They shall eat</b> — the meaning: the humble shall eat and rejoice and be sated from the abundance of joy, when they see that HaShem has saved the humble who had no helper." "And the meaning of <b>your heart shall live</b> — a man says to his fellow, in the manner of \"the spirit of Jacob their father revived\" (Genesis 45:27), for his heart was as though dead."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:17.388604260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}